# CENTRELINE are one number -- and CARD-309's 2 px differenced an ink extent
# against a path coordinate. Two orchestrator claims are RETRACTED by its
# measurement: the 0.169 mm is NOT ADR-0037/R2's device floor (a coincidence of
# two constants; R2's floor is a minimum THICKNESS), and ink-against-ink the
# grid's edges differ by 1 px = 0.0847 mm, INSIDE the bound. The figure that
# exceeds it is 3 px = 0.254 mm on Drawing.left/top, a rasteriser mitring a
# stroked `re`'s corner against Pillow's butt caps. CARD-322 therefore reds on
# the DRAWING's outer edges, not the grid's, and its repair is a centre-reading
# oracle rather than a wider tolerance.
#
# THIS FILE DID NOT PARSE until today. CARD-318's entry had lost its `- id:`,
# `phase:`, `branch:` and `worktree:` lines when it was dispatched, so its
# `started`/`note` collapsed into CARD-330's entry and ruamel refused the whole
# file with a DuplicateKeyError. Nothing read it in that state, which is why it
# went unnoticed for a day -- the dispatcher's own record is the one artefact on
# this board with no guard over it. Repaired by reconstructing CARD-318's header
# from its card file and worktree; a parse check is now part of closing a wave.
