#     cycle_2: "5.5 -- 1 critical, 2 important. Severity gate CLOSED. Report meta/review/20261023T004419Z-CARD-264-cycle2.yml (synced). The polish round verifies as good work (6 of 8 findings genuinely resolved, F-4 and F-5 CLOSED rather than declared, each re-derived by the reviewer); what the unreviewed window cost is the NARROWING MERGE's residue -- the docs page still describes the tests/test_cli.py work the fold took back to main, including a verbatim quotation of a comment that does not exist and a citation of a class present nowhere."
#     stalled_check: "FIRES on the numbers (dscore -2.8 < 0.5 AND dfindings -3 <= 0) and is OVERRIDDEN, with the reasons on the card and WITHOUT writing the literal `improvement stalled` marker -- that string is a contract with status/retrospective meaning the loop is not converging, and it would be false data here. The check's premise is that two cycles reviewed the same content; cycle 1 reviewed d40e9d4a, cycle 2 reviewed d5da18ff PLUS a merge that removed content. Cycle 1 gated on nothing, so prev_findings_count=0 is a floor against which ANY discovery trips condition (b) automatically. Corroborated independently: the FAMILY REGRESSION detector reads streak 0 -- no gating finding is attributable to the previous fix."
