#     not_in_doubt: "Full suite green at e26e5473 (8921 exec / 8894 pass / 27 skip / 0 fail). Every AC passes with on-disk plants in both states. G-1..G-7 hold, G-1 and G-6 verified two ways. CON-009 + CON-010 genuinely run, 9 passed. Cycle 3: 0 critical, 0 important, score 9.6. The card's actual deliverable is done and certified."
#     fix_4: "Committed 8727e519 (3 files, +764/-59; meta/ left out of the branch as always). The round DECIDED the tables' semantics before touching an entry -- an entry's text is exactly what was measured, keying is PER SOURCE LINE, a case constructs the declared shape missed plus the excluded neighbour caught -- then applied that tree-wide rather than to the four entries the findings named: 9 MEASURED_* assignments found by AST, 4 keyed per line (11 entries, 57 source lines), 5 exempted BY NAME WITH A REASON, with no third state permitted. 57 lines x 4 mutations = 216 variants, 0 survived, every failure naming the mutated line. 9/9 kill-matrix mutants killed, ANY-RED, both passes, domain 210 ast.Assert nodes. ONE BEHAVIOUR CHANGE, flagged rather than absorbed: m-1's mentioned() PEP-503 separator normalisation (deny-side arm, so an unseen spelling is a missed catch; the two runtime names carry no separator, so their pattern is byte-identical to the old one). FIFTH consecutive round to disagree with its brief and the SECOND to disagree with the orchestrator: the brief gave F-2's bound a three-clause form naming one of the THREE arms _classify runs before _is_type_expression, and _is_type_expression('list[bool].md') is True while _classify returns ('path', ...) -- CAUGHT -- so the brief would have declared a hole that does not exist, in cycle 1's own over-wide direction."
#     pre_gate_4: "PASSED 2026-10-23, suite lock redirected to a scratch path so the board's own lock was never read, written or created. (1) The seven tests the FIXED ids name, selected by explicit NODE ID rather than -k -- this card has twice recorded a -k selection that collected nothing and read as a pass, and a bad node id exits 4 instead of passing silently: 7 collected, 7 passed, exit 0, each named individually in the -rA listing. (2) Both touched files whole, counts compared against the round's claims: test_guard_integrity.py 167 collected / 167 passed / exit 0, test_web_server.py 166 / 166 / exit 0 -- exact match. (3) Two of the nine mutants RE-DERIVED with an instrument written at the gate rather than by re-running kill_matrix.py, honouring both measured traps explicitly (every `old` pre-counted and line-count preserving; SHIPPED's exit code read, not only its cells): SHIPPED exit 0 / 0 failed / 167 passed / no cells; MB-CENSUS killed, exit 1, 1 failed, FAIL cell :3991 = the cell claimed; F1-GUT-SHAPE killed, exit 1, 1 failed, FAIL cell :4707 = the cell claimed, which is the new per-line keying control and the load-bearing half of the round's argument. Target restored from a cp -p backup, restore verified by sha256 against the pre-run digest, git status unchanged. (4) G-6 re-verified AT THE GATE rather than taken from the round's note: no src/ path in the diff. Found one thing the round did not report: pyproject addopts already carries -q, so a -q written on a command line stacks to -qq and pytest prints NO pass/fail count line at all (measured both ways) -- absent evidence reading as zero evidence, this card's family one level out. Routed to the backlog beside its two siblings; every figure above is from a run that was not silenced."
#     gate_fix_4: "PASSED at 8727e519 -- exit 0, 8931 executed, 8904 passed, 27 skipped, 0 failed, 0 error; no duration recorded (G-7). Reconciles exactly: 8925 -> 8931 (+6) against test_guard_integrity.py 161 -> 167 (+6) and test_web_server.py 166 -> 166 (+0), the six being the six test FUNCTIONS the diff adds (enumerated by ast, not by eye). The seventh FIXED id is a MODIFIED existing test, which is why the delta is 6 and not 7. Cumulative +48 over four rounds, all accounted for. RUN TWICE, and the first run is a finding against the orchestrator: it was green and identical while holding NO LOCK, because the lock is written by the GATE SCRIPT (tests/README.md:335-339) and pytest only reads it -- I ran pytest and skipped the write, then reported the gate as locked. Nothing could have caught it: current_verdict() returns (True, None) on a missing lock because that is the normal case for every scoped run, and the guard's subject is a FOREIGN lock, so 'no lock' and 'my own lock, released' are one observation from inside the run. Re-run with the lock written per the README (holder/at/absolute worktree/commit, trap armed with the lock and disarmed in the same breath, file verified gone), and the second run MATCHED THE FIRST CELL FOR CELL -- a provenance defect, not a measurement one. Whether this card's EARLIER gates took the lock is not verifiable from here and is not asserted either way. Routed to the backlog as default-deny (ADR-0039/R2): a full run must be requirable to be covered."
#     cycle_5: "7.6 NOT CERTIFIED. 0 critical, 2 important, 2 minor. Report meta/review/20261023T103148Z-CARD-264-cycle5.yml (synced, yaml.safe_load clean). WHAT CONVERGED -- the mechanism fix 4 decided and built held under INDEPENDENT re-derivation: a 197-variant sweep over the 52 keyed lines the round's own mutants do not cover (0 survivors, 0 misattributions); a planted sixth MEASURED_* table reds the completeness arm naming the plant, so the no-third-state claim CAN fail; all five exemption reasons verified TRUE at their cited controls, with the exemption table held to an equality (10 == 10, breaking both ways); _classify default-deny by measurement; m-1 VERIFIED SOUND (byte-identity confirmed, only the two extras-only names widen, no false positive constructible); m-B's census re-derived in a NEW domain and correct; m-4's quotation exact by hand; G-1..G-7 clear with 0 banned codepoints; AC-1..AC-6 selected by node id and passed; 167/167, 166/166, 333/333 post-check. AND the fifth disagreement is adjudicated: THE ROUND WAS RIGHT, the brief (mine) was wrong -- _classify runs three arms before _is_type_expression and _is_type_expression('list[bool].md') is True while _classify returns ('path',...), caught; the clause the round added against my objection is itself controlled (deleting the path arm = 6 FAIL cells)."
#     cycle_5_gating: "F-001 tests/test_guard_integrity.py:3157 -- the contract's OWN clause 2 claims five directions (gut/invert/add/delete/move) where only four are constructed and the add/delete mechanism has NO failing control: disabling `if span != len(element_keys):` gives kill_matrix exit 0 / 210 reached / 0 FAIL and a plain run of 167 collected / 167 passed / exit 0. The add direction is constructed nowhere (the round's 216-variant sweep cannot reach it -- none of its four mutations changes an entry's line count, and the reviewer's 197-variant replication inherited the blind spot). The delete direction is SILENT on the realistic edit: a declaration line dropped together with its key gives verdict [] with every value-read assert passing, and the floor pin `assert keyed >= 45` reads 56 against a measured 57 -- eleven lines of slack -- so the contract permits the entry to shrink back to exactly the round-3 wording round 4 exists to correct. F-002 card:1604 -- 'The complete enumeration' says nine/four/11 where the tree holds ten/five/twelve, refuted by the deployed enumerator AND by the card's own table three lines below; 9/4/11 is the tree BEFORE m-A added MEASURED_UNENFORCED_PHRASE_MISSES in this same round, i.e. the headline figure predates the round's own last edit. Minors (non-gating): m-4 adds an untested line-number citation into a churning docstring in the round that removed such citations from this page; AC-7 still live in the AC block naming a test that exists nowhere (withdrawal recorded honestly at :17 and :1109)."
#     stalled_check_c5: "FIRES and is NOT overridden -- the literal marker is written this time because it is true. dscore 7.65 -> 7.6 = -0.05 (< min_improvement 0.5) AND dgating 2 -> 2 = 0 (<= 0). Unlike cycle 2, the premise HOLDS: cycles 4 and 5 reviewed the same card with one pure fix commit between them, which is exactly the comparison the check is built for. Marker: improvement stalled."
#     family_regression_c5: "FIRES at streak 2. Cycle 4's two gating findings were attributed to fix 3; cycle 5's two are attributed to fix 4; both land in one family. family_regression: on -> escalate with the family rather than spend the sixth round. UPDATED FAMILY SENTENCE -- the code converged and the record did not: each round now builds the mechanism correctly and then writes its claims ABOUT the mechanism before its own last edit, without re-deriving either against the final tree. Clause 2's five directions and the 9/4/11 census were both written before m-A landed. A different defect from cycle 4's and a cheaper one, but the fifth consecutive round in the family."
#     orchestrator_fault: "F-001 is my brief's as much as the round's. The board has a standing rule -- a fix must mutate by DELETING each mechanism its claims name, because a mutant that only breaks what the fix ADDED certifies the addition and says nothing about load-bearingness -- and grep over the fix-4 brief confirms the brief did not restate it. 8 of the round's 9 mutants mutate declaration text or a comment figure; the 9th reverts a behaviour change. I restated the rule to the cycle-5 REVIEWER and not to the round that was writing the controls. Any further fix brief on this card must carry it, plus the reviewer's own condition: the matrix MUST include an add-a-line mutant and a co-edited-drop mutant or it reproduces this cycle."
#     escalated_at_c5: 2026-10-23
#     station_c5: owner
#     owner_decision_c5: "2026-10-23 -- FIX BOTH, THEN A REVIEW SCOPED TO THE TWO FIXES (option 1 of four). F-001 takes the reviewer's SECOND option, not the first: narrowing clause 2 would make the claim true while leaving :3157 with no failing control and the entry still free to shrink back to the round-3 wording. So: add the add-a-line case and the co-edited-drop case, and replace `assert keyed >= 45` (reads 56 against a measured 57 -- eleven lines of slack, which is what lets the drop pass) with an equality over 5 tables / 12 entries / 57 lines re-derived through the deployed enumerator. Control: with :3157 disabled the new cases must RED -- that is cycle 5's surviving M2-SPAN-EQ-DROP. F-002: recompute every figure in 'The complete enumeration' through the enumerator and name the door, and restate what the 216-variant sweep does NOT cover (none of its four mutations changes an entry's line count). The brief carries, as its first instruction, the rule the fix-4 brief omitted -- a fix mutates by DELETING each mechanism its claims name -- plus the class audit: every claim in the diff that says a control reds or survives needs a constructed case per direction or must narrow."
#     owed: "fix round 5 (uncommitted hand-back, as with fix 4) -> orchestrator pre-gate -> commit -> full-suite gate WITH THE BOARD LOCK WRITTEN BY THE GATE -> narrow re-entry review of the two fixes only -> AC/EC/G verification gate -> merge gate -> merge -> remove ../PythonProject4-card-264. Aggregate round counter reaches 6 of 6; no seventh round without a fresh owner decision."
#     owner_decision: "OPTION 1, 2026-10-23: fix S-1..S-4, then a re-entry review cycle to certify, then re-gate and merge. Aggregate round counter 3 of the 6 that signal non-convergence, so cycle 4 is inside the discipline. The alternatives were merge+route-to-CARD-266 (cheapest, defensible on cost, wrong on substance -- four controls that cannot fail would ship in a card raised to remove them) and fix+ship-uncertified (the wave-48 trap by name)."
#     reversal_recorded: "I stated in-session that I would route rather than escalate, on the premise that the fix was two text narrowings. R1's two findings are MISSING CONTROLS, not text, so the premise was false and the decision is reversed on the record."
