#       WRITE, i.e. the production code was shaped to be legible to its own guard, so the guard's
#       completeness rested on discipline rather than construction -- while the legacy branch
#       three lines above wrote through .update(), invisible to the predicate. Cycle 2 (8.5, PASS)
#       then found the inversion still had an alias hole: a fresh container holding REFERENCES to
#       durable rows counted as not-durable-state, so three real grid writes left the guard green.
#       THE CARD PASSED ON SCORE AT THAT POINT AND WAS FIXED ANYWAY, because the reviewer's
#       failure scenario named CARD-246 -- the dependent card next in line -- adding a batch
#       repair that gathers rows into a local first. A hole whose concrete failure scenario is
#       "the next card does a natural thing" is a trap set for that card, not a residue.
#       The fix cycle then REFUSED the suggested remedy and demonstrated why both ways: as stated
#       it is depth-1 and misses the same defect one level down (a FOURTH shape, found by the fix
#       and not the review); applied at any depth it turns a genuine reader into a grid writer.
#       What shipped grades expressions rather than names at three levels. False positives were
#       excluded three ways, including BYTE-IDENTICAL verdict sets on the real module
