# # ---- CARD-308 to REVIEW CYCLE 1 (2026-10-29) ----
# # Branch 19bc968b, 4 commits off f64112f2, 2 files +1249: an ADR-0039 section
# # and tests/test_check_ref_resolution.py. Nothing under meta/kanban on the
# # branch, which is correct -- AC-1's config key could not land there because
# # /commit excludes meta/, so the orchestrator applied `architecture_validator`
# # to main on the round's behalf after re-verifying its claims (validate.py
# # byte-identical between the two validator copies; validators/adr_integrity.py
# # the only differing SOURCE file). The reviewer is told AC-1 is closed
# # off-branch so it is not reported as unmet.
# #
# # THE HAZARD THIS CARD IS ABOUT APPLIES TO ITS OWN REVIEWER, and the brief
# # leads with that: meta/review is not excluded from the resolver, so a review
# # report that spells a whole path::name revives that ref -- measured four times
# # now, by four routes, one of them this file and one of them the round's own
# # report. The reviewer is instructed not to spell a dead ref's whole string, to
# # use a device that the loose search cannot match, and to SAY IN THE YAML which
# # device it used. A report that revives a ref while reviewing the card about
# # refs being revived is the defect eating its own reviewer.
# #
# # WHERE THE BUDGET IS POINTED, in order:
# #   1. the self-check cell that must prove the module revives nothing -- the
# #      subtlest property here. The round got it right only after finding that
# #      routing the check through the tracked-file pass made it pass VACUOUSLY on
# #      a new file, because git ls-files cannot see an untracked one. Its
# #      truncation device is also to be verified against git grep itself rather
# #      than reasoned about, specifically against a prefix collision.
# #   2. whether count+digest pinning is a measurement or a tripwire that will be
# #      bumped, and whether repair-vs-signal-loss is ENFORCED or only written
# #      down.
# #   3. the loose resolver's prefix bug -- its trie bound `?` to one character and
# #      SILENTLY emptied three refs' hit sets, found only by diffing against a
# #      second implementation. A loose resolver that under-reports makes every
# #      class figure wrong in the safe-looking direction, so the control for it is
# #      the most important thing in the diff.
# #   4. AC-3's edge mutant, which first SURVIVED VACUOUSLY because the mutated ref
# #      dropped out of its own set -- and whether any other cell can still pass
# #      that way, which is a shape rather than a one-off.
# #
# # CENSUS DISAGREEMENT TO RECONCILE: the round derives 576 distinct refs from the
# #   four authorities; the orchestrator, deriving independently, got 580. Both
# #   agree on the shape and on 23 node-id refs. Whichever is wrong, the partition
