# # ---- CARD-285 to REVIEW CYCLE 1 (2026-10-29) ----
# # Branch af160fd5, 3 commits off 464ae377, 6 files +1583/-25. All THREE cards in
# # flight are now at review cycle 1 or past it; nothing is at implementation.
# #
# # HOST CONDITION recorded because it affects how the report should be read:
# #   load 22.25 on 11 cores with two other review cycles running. The brief tells
# #   the reviewer that a slow test is probably contention, not the card, and that
# #   hang_guard's 120s per-test ceiling _exit()s the session -- so re-measure
# #   before attributing. No lock was held at dispatch.
# #
# # WHAT THE ROUND DELIVERED, and the decision it was forced into: the card's
# #   counting item collides with CARD-283/284's own controls. Verified by the
# #   orchestrator -- FOUR shipped browser tests assert every request the page
# #   issues is same-origin, three by the literal startswith(url + "/"). A
# #   GoatCounter tag hard-written into the pages is cross-origin and would have
# #   red all four, making AC-390's load-bearing "unchanged" false by the round's
# #   own hand. So the snippet is injected at ASSEMBLY TIME, DEFAULT-OFF, and the
# #   residual is declared rather than hidden: the no-egress controls now measure
# #   the UNCOUNTED tree, with AC-390 asserting the byte difference between the
# #   counted and uncounted trees is exactly the snippet line in exactly the pages
# #   the report names.
# #
# # THE THREE REFS ARE CLOSED. Re-measured under the validator's own pathspec at
# #   the cut: AC-390 and AC-391 had ZERO resolvers, AC-392 had THREE and all three
# #   were review YAMLs -- the board's one true false alive. All three now resolve
# #   to real def lines. This also closes two of CARD-307's three honest gaps
# #   without CARD-307 being touched.
# #
# # WHERE THE REVIEW BUDGET IS POINTED:
# #   1. whether the counted-vs-uncounted byte assertion genuinely CONSTRAINS, and
# #      whether "the deployed tree is never the tested tree" is adequately covered
# #      or is itself a finding -- no browser test loads the counted tree with
# #      counting on except AC-390's own;
# #   2. the ONE existing test the round had to edit -- CARD-284's ref-bookkeeping
# #      test, which asserted the three refs were ABSENT and could not survive the
# #      card landing. The question is whether the edit KEPT ITS TEETH: can it still
# #      catch a fourth undefined ref, or was it narrowed into silence;
