# #       THE FIX THAT WOULD HAVE BEEN WRONG: widening the status set alone. The
# #       kanban skill defines `skip` as unblocking dependents "as if the
# #       dependency were done", so a parser reading the new status as merely
# #       not-done keeps every declaration naming it alive forever -- the false
# #       green that guard exists to refuse. The terminal-status set landed with
# #       it, and because no declaration names such a card today the real board
# #       cannot witness the claim, so it got four synthetic-board arms and a
