# # --- CARD-308 fix round 2 landed 3fab6828, 2026-10-29 ---
# # The gating finding is closed on all six shapes and all four authorities, and
# #   by a stronger repair than the brief asked for: each authority's scan now
# #   derives the lines it READS from one shared region helper, and any
# #   declaration key no narrow pattern claims hits a default-deny naming file,
# #   line and text. Collection and refusal cannot drift apart because both come
# #   from one notion of where a declaration lives.
# #   Proof is a MATRIX: 26 illegal shapes at all four authorities against a
# #   synthetic authority set, PLUS 4 legal shapes asserted to still derive their
# #   ref -- without those, a derivation that raised on everything would pass
# #   every negative case while reading nothing. Cycle 2's false green was
# #   reproduced and then killed.
# #   THE SHARPER RULE IT STATES, and the card's real lesson: a cross-reading is
# #   not a default-deny. Two readings of the same assumption about where refs
# #   live agreed on a figure and were BOTH wrong.
# #
# # TWO HOLES IT FOUND THAT NEITHER MY BRIEF NOR THE REVIEW NAMED:
# #   (a) a declaration-key default-deny needs a region notion or it reds on
# #       ENGLISH, and the shape is live today -- exactly one declaration-shaped
# #       line in the ADR set sits outside a fence and it is a wrapped prose
# #       sentence, which arrived with main's own recent ADR edit. A naive
# #       anchored default-deny would have reded the suite on it.
# #   (b) the opposite failure already existed and is worse for a census: the
# #       narrow pattern was COLLECTING a wrapped prose line from inside a block
# #       scalar AS A REF. A guard that invents a ref out of prose corrupts the
# #       census in the direction nothing else here checks.
# #
# # ITS REPAIR OF THE "UNENFORCEABLE" CLAIM WAS DEMONSTRATED ON THE REAL EVENT:
# #   per-member digests recover a departed member BY NAME and judge the departure,
# #   and replayed against the live move it names both departed refs as SIGNAL
# #   LOSS with no definition anywhere. That is this card's instrument detecting,
# #   on live data, the very thing I did to the board earlier today.
# #
# # TWO OF MY OWN FIGURES WERE WRONG IN THE BRIEF, and the second is the lesson:
# #   an ADR path with a doubled segment, and an occurrence count that was right
# #   at the review's tree and STALE at HEAD because main's edit moved it. Pasting
# #   it would have written a wrong number into the ADR -- the exact failure the
# #   brief warned about, demonstrated on the brief. It re-derived at three
# #   revisions with two independent instruments instead.
# #   It also made the review's non-summing decomposition sum, by finding the
# #   overlap the review had missed.
# #   And it REMOVED one figure rather than correcting it, because the quantity is
# #   unstatable: the sentence stating it contains ellipses of its own and so
# #   changes what it reports. Replaced by the property, derived on every run.
# #
# # IT SELF-REPORTED A PROCESS ERROR rather than hiding it: it ran a stash on the
