# # THE MERGE IS A MERGE COMMIT, NOT A FAST-FORWARD, and the gate's coverage of
# #   the merged tree is PROVED rather than argued: the src/ and tests/ tree hashes
# #   in the merged commit are byte-identical to the gated commit's on both sides.
# #   That is the check an arithmetic reconciliation cannot give, and it is the
# #   right answer to a question this board has previously answered by addition.
# #
# # THREE CYCLES EACH FOUND A SILENT PASS THE PREVIOUS ONE MISSED -- one, then
# #   four, then four more of a different class. The last class was the sharpest:
# #   the pattern the design called internal-only actually routes a protocol-
# #   relative target to the egress bucket, while its raw counterpart demanded a
# #   dotted letter-TLD authority -- so single-label, bracketed-IPv6, encoded,
# #   userinfo and port-only authorities were readable only through the stripped
